    "designMd": "---\nname: Veritalex\ncolors:\n  surface: '#fff8f5'\n  surface-dim: '#e4d8d1'\n  surface-bright: '#fff8f5'\n  surface-container-lowest: '#ffffff'\n  surface-container-low: '#FCF1E8'\n  surface-container: '#F5E9DF'\n  surface-container-high: '#EEE1D5'\n  surface-container-highest: '#ede0d9'\n  on-surface: '#241A14'\n  on-surface-variant: '#55483D'\n  inverse-surface: '#362f2b'\n  inverse-on-surface: '#fbeee7'\n  outline: '#857469'\n  outline-variant: '#d7c3b6'\n  surface-tint: '#895021'\n  primary: '#6c390b'\n  on-primary: '#ffffff'\n  primary-container: '#FFDCBF'\n  on-primary-container: '#2D1606'\n  inverse-primary: '#ffb782'\n  secondary: '#6e5b4b'\n  on-secondary: '#ffffff'\n  secondary-container: '#f9ddc9'\n  on-secondary-container: '#756050'\n  tertiary: '#5D633D'\n  on-tertiary: '#ffffff'\n  tertiary-container: '#E1E8B8'\n  on-tertiary-container: '#98e4f7'\n  error: '#ba1a1a'\n  on-error: '#ffffff'\n  error-container: '#ffdad6'\n  on-error-container: '#93000a'\n  primary-fixed: '#ffdcc5'\n  primary-fixed-dim: '#ffb782'\n  on-primary-fixed: '#301400'\n  on-primary-fixed-variant: '#6d390b'\n  secondary-fixed: '#f9ddc9'\n  secondary-fixed-dim: '#dcc2ae'\n  on-secondary-fixed: '#27190c'\n  on-secondary-fixed-variant: '#554334'\n  tertiary-fixed: '#a6eeff'\n  tertiary-fixed-dim: '#86d2e4'\n  on-tertiary-fixed: '#001f25'\n  on-tertiary-fixed-variant: '#004e5b'\n  background: '#fff8f5'\n  on-background: '#201a16'\n  surface-variant: '#ede0d9'\n  surface-paper: '#FFF8F3'\n  highlight: '#F6E5A8'\ntypography:\n  headline-lg:\n    fontFamily: Roboto Flex\n    fontSize: 32px\n    fontWeight: '500'\n    lineHeight: 40px\n  headline-md:\n    fontFamily: Roboto Flex\n    fontSize: 24px\n    fontWeight: '500'\n    lineHeight: 32px\n  headline-sm:\n    fontFamily: Roboto Flex\n    fontSize: 20px\n    fontWeight: '500'\n    lineHeight: 28px\n  title-md:\n    fontFamily: Roboto Flex\n    fontSize: 16px\n    fontWeight: '500'\n    lineHeight: 24px\n  body-lg:\n    fontFamily: Roboto Flex\n    fontSize: 16px\n    fontWeight: '400'\n    lineHeight: 24px\n  body-sm:\n    fontFamily: Roboto Flex\n    fontSize: 14px\n    fontWeight: '400'\n    lineHeight: 20px\n  label-md:\n    fontFamily: Roboto Flex\n    fontSize: 14px\n    fontWeight: '500'\n    lineHeight: 20px\n  reader-prose:\n    fontFamily: Literata\n    fontSize: 19px\n    fontWeight: '400'\n    lineHeight: 32px\n  reader-chapter:\n    fontFamily: Literata\n    fontSize: 26px\n    fontWeight: '500'\n    lineHeight: 34px\nrounded:\n  sm: 0.25rem\n  DEFAULT: 0.5rem\n  md: 0.75rem\n  lg: 1rem\n  xl: 1.5rem\n  full: 9999px\nspacing:\n  gutter: 20px\n  margin: 20px\n  space-xs: 4px\n  space-sm: 8px\n  space-md: 12px\n  space-lg: 16px\n  space-xl: 24px\n  space-xxl: 32px\n---\n\n## Brand & Style\n\nThis design system establishes a calm, personal reading sanctuary rooted in the principles of Material 3 and Material You. The brand personality is scholarly, deliberate, warm, and focused entirely on the intimacy of text. It evokes the quiet focus of a personal study or a well-lit library alcove. \n\nThe aesthetic style is a refined, content-first **Corporate / Modern** execution tailored for literature:\n- **Atmospheric Warmth:** Built on warm paper tones and rich amber-brown seed colors rather than cold corporate neutrals.\n- **Utilitarian Clarity:** Strict adherence to native Android component behavior with generous whitespace and zero decorative fluff.\n- **Distraction-Free Focus:** Complete absence of marketing heroes, dashboard metrics, social feeds, or gradients.\n\n## Colors\n\nThe color palette is derived from an amber-brown brand seed (`#895021`), translating physical book-binding and warm paper into digital screens. The interface operates on warm paper surfaces that reduce eye strain during extended reading sessions.\n\n- **Primary:** Deep amber brown (`#895021`), used for primary actions, selected navigation states, and key interactive elements.\n- **Surfaces:** A progression of warm paper tones (`#FFF8F3` down to `#EEE1D5`) providing subtle tonal layering without relying on heavy borders or artificial elevation.\n- **Ink & Legibility:** Dark ink (`#241A14`) on-surface colors guarantee high contrast and crisp readability.\n- **System Adaptability:** Fully supports dynamic color systems and system light/dark modes, with independent Light, Sepia, and Dark themes available within the dedicated reading environment.\n\n## Typography\n\nTypography strictly bifurcates the application interface from the reading experience:\n- **Interface:** **Roboto Flex** is used exclusively for all app chrome, navigation, lists, headings, and metadata. Headings use medium weights (24/32 and 20/28), while body and supporting labels maintain high legibility at 16/24 and 14/20. Sentence-case labels are preferred.\n- **Book Prose:** **Literata** is reserved solely for actual book prose, chapter headings, and meaningful excerpts. The default reading size is set to a comfortable 19/32 regular grid with generous line height.\n\n## Layout & Spacing\n\nThe layout model follows a fluid Android phone baseline (optimized for 412dp, validating down to 360dp) utilizing edge-to-edge display with safe status and navigation insets. \n\n- **Grid & Gutters:** Content uses 20dp gutters (16dp on compact viewports). \n- **Spacing Rhythm:** Based on a strict 4dp/8dp scale (`4`, `8`, `12`, `16`, `24`, `32dp`), ensuring consistent vertical rhythm between section headers, book rows, and shelves.\n- **Form Factors:** On tablets, the layout expands gracefully using a navigation rail and intentional list/detail panes, restricting the central reading measure to an optimal 60-70 characters per line. Top bars are structured at 64dp and bottom navigation at 80dp plus system insets.\n\n## Elevation & Depth\n\nDepth is conveyed primarily through **Tonal Layers** rather than heavy drop shadows. \n- **Surface Tiers:** UI elements stack cleanly using the warm paper surface container hierarchy (`surface-container-low`, `surface-container`, `surface-container-high`).\n- **Shadows:** Applied strictly as transient overlays for floating action buttons, active bottom sheets, or dialog modals. \n- **Borders & Outlines:** Low-contrast outlines (`#857468`, `#D7C3B4`) bound interactive elements cleanly without card-in-card visual noise.\n\n## Shapes\n\nThe shape language utilizes friendly, approachable rounded geometry that mimics soft paper goods:\n- **Cards & Containers:** Softly rounded with a standard `16dp` radius for book cards and content blocks.\n- **Sheets & Dialogs:** Employs a larger `28dp` corner radius for bottom sheets and modal dialogs.\n- **Book Covers & Imagery:** Strictly maintains a `4dp` subtle rounding on book covers to preserve their authentic portrait ratio (approx. 2:3).\n- **Interactive Controls:** Buttons, chips, and input fields utilize pill shapes or fully rounded pill containers to encourage clear touch targets (minimum 48dp).\n\n## Components\n\nComponents follow native Material 3 guidelines, emphasizing functional clarity and touch ergonomics:\n\n- **Buttons:** Filled, tonal, and text variants with a pill main action shape. All interactive touch targets maintain a strict minimum of 48dp. Icon buttons have explicit 48dp bounds.\n- **Navigation:** Bottom navigation uses labeled destinations with a selected tonal pill indicator. The app features three primary destinations (Home, Explore, Library), with Settings housed as a toolbar action.\n- **Cards & Lists:** `BookCoverCard` components preserve accurate 2:3 portrait dimensions with dignified typeset fallbacks. `BookListRow` and `ShelfRow` components use flat tonal grouping with generous section spacing.\n- **Reader Interface:** Distraction-free text view with access to the `ReaderToolbar` and `ReaderAppearanceSheet` on tap. Supports continuous scroll and page modes seamlessly.\n- **State & Feedback:** Clear, factual status components (`DownloadState`, `SyncStatusRow`, `EmptyState`, `RetryState`) that keep users informed of offline capability and device sync status without exposing backend jargon.",
